ction. Meanwhile, former Chancellor Angela Merkel has urged people not to take democracy for granted. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The 'end of an era' as Goethe-Institut in Russia closes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a88a3b7a725a2df42d1e7f7aaf1a25496246a9b035150131735cf1348726f0d</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321--189393464061.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Goethe-Institut was one of the last German institutions still operating in Russia. However, following Moscow's decision to close its offices, all employees will have to stop working by September 13.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Cambodia's floating schools hit by rising fuel costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8e46e7298d7e1c66eefa9b7542980b959351a63b045fa2095ee8b5c4876687f</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008--dc2e9aeeea22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Iran war has sent fuel prices higher in Cambodia, squeezing families who rely on fishing and boats for their livelihoods. For children living on Tonle Sap, rising fuel costs pose yet another barrier to education.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb2ae01da0f689c349308c3c5aff89bb5f7de34bcee901147b7d544677753388</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--ac3bd047b864.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. But over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How Belarusians still find hope in a silenced country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dff7bfc9eaacb32a829782d22e1c2ee5e86bd149b2bfd76e1e3ff5dafaa0f008</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285--d234556fa838.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The documentary "Letters from the Silenced Country" depicts the ongoing repression under the authoritarian regime. Director Andrei Kutsila talked to DW ahead of the film's Venice premiere.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>The Bayeux Tapestry in London: What's behind the hype?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:42e18cd84e1dc5e66d6ee277d71fa68b969c41faaab6cce1219c938da6cdbbb0</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-bayeux-tapestry-in-london-what-s-behind-the-hype/a-78488629--9a9477f8929c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-bayeux-tapestry-in-london-what-s-behind-the-hype/a-78488629?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The exhibition of the Bayeux Tapestry at the British Museum is eagerly anticipated across the UK, as the medieval masterpiece is considered by many to be a symbol of the country's identity.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae1210e49270c6443f47d2f6eb7020abe60c30ab8dd1ec06f4c6aaf45ab8ee69</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:32Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--1ca180b39c00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s Goethe-Institut is closing in Russia. Russians tell DW how canceled exams are upending their plans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f560cf7779b676b578cef21078c8d7802b74661885a9ad758460cb6d9adcf56</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T16:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-goethe-institut-is-closing-in-russia-russians-tell-dw-how-canceled-exams-are-upending-thei/a-79218936--791b0bcb39e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-goethe-institut-is-closing-in-russia-russians-tell-dw-how-canceled-exams-are-upending-their-plans/a-79218936?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canceled language exams, disrupted plans to study in Germany and the disappearance of an important cultural link: DW users shared how the closure of Germany's Goethe-Institut in Russia affects their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><tit